      "en": "Let $H=L^2(0,1)$ and let\\[\\mathcal{D}(A)=\\{u\\in H^2(0,1)\\mid u(0)=u'(0)=u(1)=0\\}.\\]Here the boundary conditions are taken in the sense of trace. Define $A:\\mathcal{D}(A)\\to H$ by\\[A(u):=-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}^2u}{\\mathrm{d}x^2}.\\]Find the Hilbert adjoint of $(\\mathcal{D}(A),A)$. Is the operator symmetric, self-adjoint?",
      "zh": "设 $H=L^2(0,1)$, 并令\\[\\mathcal{D}(A)=\\{u\\in H^2(0,1)\\mid u(0)=u'(0)=u(1)=0\\}.\\]这里的边界条件在迹的意义下理解. 用下式定义 $A:\\mathcal{D}(A)\\to H$:\\[A(u):=-\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}^2u}{\\mathrm{d}x^2}.\\]求 $(\\mathcal{D}(A),A)$ 的 Hilbert 伴随. 该算子是否对称, 是否自伴随?",
      "label": "ex:second-derivative-symmetric-not-self-adjoint",
